what if I'm not using @Configuration but having @Bean inside the class?

🔹 Case 1: Class Has @Bean But No Spring Annotation At All
    👉 Result:
        ❌ Spring will NOT detect this class
        ❌ @Bean method will NEVER be called
        ❌ No bean is registered

🔹 Case 2: Class Has @Component But NOT @Configuration
    👉 Result:
        ✅ Spring WILL detect the class
        ✅ @Bean method WILL be processed
        ⚠ BUT important difference exists

    This is called "Lite mode" configuration.

🔹 What Is the Difference?
    There are two modes:

    1️⃣ Full Mode (@Configuration)

        Spring creates a CGLIB proxy of the class.
        This ensures:
            @Bean methods return singleton beans
            Calling one @Bean method from another does NOT create a new object

    2️⃣ Lite Mode (@Component only)
        No CGLIB proxy.
        If one @Bean method calls another:

🔹 Internally What Happens?

With @Configuration:
Spring does:
    Create subclass proxy using CGLIB
    Override @Bean methods
    Intercept calls
    Return container-managed singleton

🔥 Very Important Rule
    If your class contains @Bean methods:
    Always annotate it with @Configuration
    Even though @Component works, it is not safe for complex configurations.
